# Exclusions for CrossOver (the Steam bottle, D3DMetal 3.0 for D3D10-12 and DXGI,
# wined3d for D3D9):
#   ./dxcts run --per-group --backend d3dmetal --exclusion crossover
# One flat JSON object per line; "reason" is required.  See docs/exclusions.md.
{"binary":"WGF11SharedResources.exe","reason":"Exhausted host GPU memory on the D3DMetal backend (suites/exclusions/d3dmetal.jsonl: Metal Insufficient Memory, kIOGPUCommandBufferCallbackErrorOutOfMemory, and a host kernel panic on 2026-09-04), with the same D3DMetal 3.0 binary CrossOver runs.  Not run here to find out whether CrossOver does the same, since a host GPU fault is a host-panic risk: CrossOver ran it on 2026-10-16 without a fault, but with an older harness under which most of its groups failed in setup (3,642 cases, 15 passing).","evidence":"WGF11SharedResources in the full sweeps of 2026-10-15 on Neptune and on CrossOver"}
{"binary":"D3DConf_12_Core.dll","group":"D3DConf_12_0_ResourceBinding","reason":"Hung the host GPU three runs out of three on the D3DMetal backend (suites/exclusions/d3dmetal.jsonl: kIOGPUCommandBufferCallbackErrorHang), with the same D3DMetal 3.0 binary CrossOver runs.  Not run here to find out whether CrossOver does the same, since a host GPU hang is a host-panic risk.  Nothing here says either way: on 2026-10-16 every one of its 294 cases failed in setup within 2.5 s, before any GPU work, and the hang coincided with heap imports from guest shared memory, which CrossOver does not have.","evidence":"D3DConf_12_Core in the Neptune D3DMetal sweep of 2026-10-18 to 2026-10-20, every attempt; D3DConf_12_Core in the CrossOver full sweep of 2026-10-15"}
{"binary":"D3DConf_12_Core.dll","group":"D3DConf_12_0_DebugLayerScenarios","cases":"NonResourceStateValidation*","reason":"Exhausted host GPU memory on the D3DMetal backend (suites/exclusions/d3dmetal.jsonl: Metal Insufficient Memory, after libmetalirconverter SIGSEGVs row after row), with the same D3DMetal 3.0 binary CrossOver runs.  Not run here to find out whether CrossOver does the same, since a host GPU fault is a host-panic risk.  On 2026-10-16 the class failed in setup within 2.6 s, so nothing here says either way.","evidence":"D3DConf_12_Core in the Neptune D3DMetal sweep, the out-of-memory attempt of 2026-10-20; D3DConf_12_Core in the CrossOver full sweep of 2026-10-15"}
{"binary":"D3DConf_12_Core.dll","group":"D3DConf_12_0_IndirectDraw","cases":"IndirectDrawTest#0 Commands,IndirectDrawTestVM#0 Commands","reason":"Never returns: an ExecuteIndirect of zero commands leaves the test waiting forever (0% CPU) until the group's timeout, and every case after it in the class is lost.  The same two cases, and only those, hang on every run here (2026-10-16 without the layer, 2026-10-22 with it); with both left out the class completes in seconds with 52 cases.  On the D3DMetal backend through Neptune they fail in under a second.","evidence":"Single-case hang probes on CrossOver, 2026-10-22, one hung case left out per round; the D3DConf_12_Core proof run of the same day"}
{"binary":"D3DConf_12_Core.dll","group":"DxilConfTest","cases":"IsNormalTest","reason":"Never returns: the test waits forever for a pipeline whose compile makes Apple's MTLCompilerService abort (llvm::report_fatal_error in the AGX backend, three MTLCompilerService crash reports per run, responsible process TE.exe), until the group's timeout, and every case after it is lost.  Hangs on every run here (2026-10-16, 2026-10-22); with it left out the class completes with 203 cases, 172 passing.","evidence":"Single-case hang probes on CrossOver, 2026-10-22; MTLCompilerService crash reports from 00:33 that day"}
{"binary":"D3DConf_12_Core.dll","group":"D3DConf_12_0_MeshShaders#?#?","reason":"Never returns: every mesh-shader pipeline these classes create blocks in D3DMetal's CreatePipelineState (stream form) for good, the process idle at 0% CPU, so each case costs the group's whole timeout.  Probed one case at a time in MeshShaders#0#0, each of its first six cases hung in turn (SmallMesh, SmallMeshWithAmplification, MediumMesh, MediumMeshWithAmplification, LargeMesh, LargeMeshWithAmplification); all four classes hang at their first case on every run (2026-10-16, 2026-10-22).  On the D3DMetal backend through Neptune the same pipelines kill the render worker (SIGSEGV) and every case fails.","evidence":"Single-case hang probes of D3DConf_12_0_MeshShaders#0#0 on CrossOver, 2026-10-22 (every probed case hangs); the D3DConf_12_Core proof run of the same day"}
{"binary":"D3DConf_12_Core.dll","group":"D3DConf_12_0_MeshShaders4","cases":"MSPrimitivesPipelineStatisticIncludesCulledPrimitives_Capability","reason":"Never returns: its mesh-shader pipeline create blocks in D3DMetal for good (as in the MeshShaders#?#? classes), until the group's timeout.  Hangs on every run here (2026-10-16, 2026-10-22); it fails on the D3DMetal backend through Neptune.","evidence":"A single-case hang probe on CrossOver, 2026-10-22"}
{"binary":"ColorFill.exe","group":"ColorFillTest","reason":"Never returns: after about 365 of its 3,602 cases wined3d's command-stream thread blocks for good inside opengl32, called from wined3d's wglMakeCurrent, with the main thread waiting on it at 0% CPU, until the group's timeout; it is the binary's only group.  Hangs on every run here (2026-10-22: the wgf9 arm after 365 cases, two direct runs after 362 and 366, the second with cases 362-372 left out).","evidence":"Hang probes on CrossOver, 2026-10-22; ColorFill in the CrossOver D3D9-era sweep of that day"}
{"binary":"LockDpth.exe","group":"LockDepth","reason":"Never returns: Wine creates a D3DFMT_D32F_LOCKABLE depth surface without CPU access, so LockRect fails (wined3d: 'Resource does not have MAP_R access'); the test writes through the pointer it never got, its exception handlers fault in turn until the stack overflows, and Wine ends the main thread but not the process.  Hangs after case 48 on every run here (2026-10-22: the wgf9 arm and five direct runs), including with every case from 49 on left out, since the failing setup runs regardless.","evidence":"Hang probes on CrossOver, 2026-10-22; LockDpth in the CrossOver D3D9-era sweep of that day"}
{"binary":"LostDev.exe","group":"LostTexture","reason":"Never returns in two runs out of three: as in ColorFill, wined3d's command-stream thread blocks inside opengl32 under wglMakeCurrent with the test waiting on it.  The device is never lost here (a second LostDev.exe calling ChangeDisplaySettings does not lose a wined3d device), so nearly every case is Blocked whether or not it hangs.  2026-10-22: wedged in the wgf9 arm after 717 cases and under the runner after 384; the third run ran 974 cases, 966 Blocked, in 599 s.","evidence":"Hang probes on CrossOver, 2026-10-22; LostDev in the CrossOver D3D9-era sweep of that day"}
{"binary":"LostDev.exe","group":"LostDepthStencil","reason":"Never returns in two runs out of six under the runner (the same wglMakeCurrent block as LostTexture, backtrace in the evidence), after its first case reports the device was not lost; the other runs finish in 18 s with 10 of 12 cases passing.","evidence":"Hang probes on CrossOver, 2026-10-22; LostDev in the CrossOver D3D9-era sweep of that day"}
{"binary":"LostDev.exe","group":"LostVertexBuffer","reason":"Never returns once the D3D9-era framework runs it as Direct3D 9.1, as it does on Windows: three runs out of three hang after the same 293 passes, in the wglMakeCurrent block LostTexture hits (wined3d's command-stream thread inside opengl32, the test in d3d9 waiting on it).  As 9.0 it ran its 1,168 cases with 12 passes, the device never being lost.","evidence":"Hang probes on CrossOver, 2026-10-22; LostDev in the CrossOver D3D9-era sweep run at Direct3D 9.1"}
